# Connection events (docs/radio-tables.md 7.79, 7.80). QEMU: the hardware-configuration Peripheral
# (tests/radio-port, prj-connection.conf) against the hardware-configuration Central
# (tests/radio-rx-port, prj-central.conf), efr32bg22-dual, -icount shift=3, 120 s wall (~1200 s
# virtual), CONFIG_EFR32_RADIO_TIMING_PROBE maxima over both devices. Silicon: the explorer kit as
# Peripheral (tests/radio-port, prj-hardware.conf + GATT test + probes, admission off and misses
# counted) connected from the host's controller: one connection that ended at its supervision
# timeout (7.80), so a small sample: those defaults are the longest seen in it, and the close
# budget keeps the QEMU figure (the silicon close seen, 31.1 us, was not an abort after RX).
# 7.84: connections that hold (laptop Central, 45 ms interval, GATT every second, 5 min each,
# unencrypted and encrypted, probes read only after the link closed); where their maxima exceed
# the 7.80 figures the defaults are now theirs. Closes seen there: last TX 63.4 us, abort 36.4 us;
# the close budget still keeps the QEMU figure.

