config EFR32_RADIO_WAKE_LATENCY_NS
	int "Clock-event wake to job dispatch (ns)"
	default 55700
	help
	  A timed command job (TX launch, QEMU TIFS turnaround) is armed this
	  much before its not-before bound; admission models any other timed
	  release as starting this late. The steady-state TIMER0 interrupt
	  without admission (39.4 us) and the TX launch's longest
	  release-to-start (16.3 us), silicon. With admission on, every TX
	  launch on silicon (and in QEMU) was dispatched before its bound: the
	  expiry is delivered within 18.3 us (QEMU 31.9 us) and the job starts
	  at most EFR32_RADIO_SPIN_EXIT_NS after the bound.

config EFR32_RADIO_TIMING_PROBE
	bool "Record the longest radio job paths for a debugger"
	help
